openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: PicEte Image Processing API
  description: |
    PicEte is a client-side image processing tool. There is no server-side API.
    All processing is done via the browser's Canvas API.

    An AI agent can use PicEte by controlling a headless browser (Playwright, Puppeteer, etc.)
    to navigate to the tool pages, upload images, configure options, and download results.

    The steps are the same for all tools:
    1. Navigate to the tool page
    2. Upload an image via file input
    3. Configure options (format, quality, dimensions)
    4. Click process button
    5. Wait for the download section to appear
    6. Download the processed image
  version: 1.0.0
servers:
  - url: https://picete.com
    description: Production

paths:
  /:
    summary: Home page — general image converter
    description: Drop zone with format selector (JPEG/PNG/WebP), quality slider (10-100), width/height inputs with aspect ratio lock, and process/download buttons.
    browser_steps:
      - upload: click select button (#selectBtn) or drag-and-drop onto #uploadArea
      - config_format: click one of format-option labels (jpeg/png/webp)
      - config_quality: drag #qualitySlider or set .value
      - config_size: fill #widthInput and #heightInput, check #maintainAspect
      - process: click #processBtn
      - download: wait for #downloadSection to appear, click download buttons

  /png-to-jpg/:
    summary: Convert PNG to JPG
    description: Upload PNG files and download as JPEG. Quality slider controls JPG compression.

  /jpg-to-png/:
    summary: Convert JPG to PNG
    description: Upload JPG files and download as PNG (lossless).

  /webp-to-png/:
    summary: Convert WebP to PNG
    description: Upload WebP files and download as PNG. Preserves transparency.

  /png-to-webp/:
    summary: Convert PNG to WebP
    description: Upload PNG files and download as WebP. Smaller file size, good web format.

  /jpg-to-webp/:
    summary: Convert JPG to WebP
    description: Upload JPG files and download as WebP. Good compression for web use.

  /resize-image/:
    summary: Resize images
    description: Upload images and set custom width/height. Maintain aspect ratio option.

  /compress-image/:
    summary: Compress images
    description: Upload images and adjust quality slider to reduce file size while maintaining quality.

x-claude-model-description: >
  PicEte is a free online image processing toolkit. All operations run client-side
  in the browser using Canvas API. No images are ever uploaded to any server.

  To use PicEte programmatically, control a headless browser instance and:
  1. Navigate to the desired tool page
  2. Upload the image file via the file input element (#fileInput)
  3. Set options via the UI controls (radio buttons, sliders, number inputs)
  4. Click the process button
  5. Download the result

  All tool pages follow the same interaction pattern.
